{"sourceSha256": "ab429bbd290d251b1cc1e56f9b7f7367c9551f0fe7e8554b218edc6a82b372cd", "text": "OCCUPATIONAL ENGLISH TEST\nWRTING SUB-TEST:                      MEDICINE\nTIME ALLOWED:                       READING TIME: 5 MINUTES\n                                     WRITING TIME:40 MINUTES\nRead the case notes below and complete the writing task which follows\n\nNotes:\nMr Kenny Stewart is a 60 year old gentleman presenting in your general practice with a swollen left big\ntoe.\n\nPatient:           Kenny Stewart\n\nResidence:         118 Wharncliffe Drive\n\n                    Surrey,London,UK\n\nDOB:                17.5.1962\n\nSOCIAL HISTORY: Retired nurse\n\n                    Married, 2 adult children\n\n                    Never smoked\n\n                     Binge drinking 17 units of ETOH/weekly\n\nObservations:        BP 110/80 mmHg HR 76 bpm\n\n                     RR 16/MIN\n\n                     Afebrile to touch\n\nFHx:                Father - Died in RTA (40 Years )\n\n                     Mother- Died in Childbirth\n\n                     Unknown history for grandparents\n\n                     Brother – Rheumatoid Arthritis (RA)\n\f\nPMx :               Low birth weight Inguinal\n\n                    Hernia (2008) Annual\n\n                    Influenza Vaccine\n\n                    Previous diagnosis of Gout - lost to follow up (2009)\n\nMedications:        None\n\n                     Previously Offered\n\n                     NSAID’S – Stopped by patient\n\nTreatment record:\n\n20.4.19:            2 weeks history of cough and cold symptoms\n\n                     Found to be febrile, WCC = 18,000\n\n                     Started on 7 day course - Amoxyclav PO\n\n                     Resolved symptoms on follow up\n\n20.5.2019:          Attended for follow up visit\n\n                    Chest X Ray NAD\n\n30.6.19:            2 Weeks H/O Swollen knee joint (Rt)\n\n                    Joint Aspiration – Suggestive of gouty arthritis\n\n                    Started on Colchicine 500mg TDS x 2 weeks\n\n31.6.19:            Patient attended with abdominal cramps and watery diarrhea.\n\n                    ? Drug induced : Advised to continue prescribed medication at\n\n                     BD dose +PRN Loperamide\n\n7.9.2019:           Annual Influenza Vaccine\n\n10.10.19:           Re-attended with swollen left toe\n\n                    Patient very anxious re: RA in brother\n\f\nPatient would not live to wait for rheumatology appointment\n\n                  Wants to be treated by private GP\n\n                  Patient counseled and referred by urgent Rheumatology appointment\n\n                   (1 week wait)\n\n                  Bloods done\n\n0/E:              GOUTY Tophi Left ear, vitals NAD\n\n                  Left knee( Swollen, red, warm to touch), left toe ( swollen ,red, warm to touch)\n\n                  Mild Eczema (face) - has tried new facial\n\nInvestigations:     Hb       118/dl (115 – 165/dl)\n\n                   RBC       4.5 (3.80 – 5.50 )\n\n                   PCV       0.40\n\n                   MCV        79\n\n                    WCC         14,000\n\n                   Neutrophils 11,000(78% )\n\n                   X Ray Left Toe :- Mouse bitten appearance\n\n\nWriting Task: Using the information above, write a letter of referral requesting an urgent\n\nappointment to Dr Wysozynski, Consultant Rheumatology, Kentucky Hospital, USA. Make\n\nsure you mention secondary prevention in view of recurrent attendances.", "pages": [{"number": 1, "text": "OCCUPATIONAL ENGLISH TEST\nWRTING SUB-TEST:                      MEDICINE\nTIME ALLOWED:                       READING TIME: 5 MINUTES\n                                     WRITING TIME:40 MINUTES\nRead the case notes below and complete the writing task which follows\n\nNotes:\nMr Kenny Stewart is a 60 year old gentleman presenting in your general practice with a swollen left big\ntoe.\n\nPatient:           Kenny Stewart\n\nResidence:       